  "id": "DrugBank_DB00877 - MONDO_5086",
  "verbalization": "Sirolimus, a mTOR inhibitor, is implicated in the treatment of Nonpapillary Renal Cell Carcinoma through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Sirolimus is linked to Renal Cell Carcinoma (disease) via the indications of Nonpapillary Renal Cell Carcinoma, which in turn are associated with other targeted therapies such as Tivozanib, Axitinib, and Cabozantinib. These drugs are often used in the management of renal cell carcinoma, and their association with the disease implies a potential role in its treatment. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Sirolimus may influence the progression or treatment of renal cell carcinoma, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a relationship between Sirolimus and renal cell carcinoma through its involvement in the treatment of related malignancies, suggesting a potential therapeutic role in this context.",
